codex
The new design-status gate has bypass/enforcement gaps: malformed frontmatter can pass, and the legacy-value ratchet is only advisory when it should prevent regressions. These issues undermine the patch's stated CI guard behavior.

Full review comments:

- [P2] Reject unterminated frontmatter blocks — /home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/doc-hygiene-2/scripts/lint-design-status.sh:91-92
  When a `dev/design` file starts with `---` but never closes the YAML block, this `awk` reads the rest of the document as `block`, so any later `status:` line in the body makes the file pass even though it has no valid YAML frontmatter. This leaves the new gate bypassable for malformed docs; track whether the closing `---` was actually found and fail otherwise.

- [P2] Enforce the legacy ratchet when the count drops — /home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/doc-hygiene-2/scripts/lint-design-status.sh:146-148
  If a cleanup reduces `LEGACY_SEEN` below `LEGACY_BUDGET`, this only emits a notice and still exits successfully, so the stale ceiling can remain and a later PR can add legacy statuses back up to that old budget without failing. Since this is intended to be a monotone ratchet, the below-budget case needs to fail (or otherwise block) until the budget is lowered in the same change.
